{"Annotation cleanup logs at Error level on the success path and prints full ID batches and SQL conditions, which can flood production error logs and become expensive with large batch sizes": 0.9683805108070374, "The global cleanup loop ticker was changed from 10 minutes to 1 minute, increasing how often all cleanup tasks run and contradicting existing documentation that states temp CSV/PNG cleanup runs every 10 minutes": 0.9369686245918274, "The new split SELECT+DELETE approach can still share the same DB session/transaction when the context already contains a session, undermining the stated goal of letting locks flush between statements": 0.6790267825126648, "Integration test registers t.Cleanup after data creation and fatal assertions, so a failure in setup/assertions can leave tables dirty and break later subtests that reuse the same DB handle": 0.7394257187843323}